# Site configuration for scripts/lsf.
#
# Copy this to site.conf next to the scripts (it is gitignored), or point
# SLASH_LSF_SITE_CONF at a copy on shared storage to share one configuration
# across a team. Every value below is specific to a particular cluster, which
# is why none of them are baked into the repository.
#
# The ":=" form means an already-exported value wins, so a one-off override
# such as
#
#     SLASH_LSF_MEM_MB=120000 slashkit link ...
#
# still works -- and beats the per-task values further down, so that the
# override actually takes effect.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- cluster ---

# The queue to submit to. Pick one whose limits fit a multi-hour, many-GB job;
# a default queue is usually not it.
: "${SLASH_LSF_QUEUE:=<your-queue>}"

# Added as -R "select[ostype==...]". Leave empty to omit the clause entirely.
# Worth setting if the farm is mixed and the tools only support some of it.
: "${SLASH_LSF_OSTYPE:=}"

# Sourced on the submit host if bsub is not already on PATH. Leave empty if
# the LSF commands are always available.
: "${SLASH_LSF_PROFILE:=}"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ tools ---

# Sourced on the execution host to put the tools on PATH. This must be the
# bash flavour: LSF runs the job as a non-interactive script under bash, where
# settings64.csh fails with "setenv: command not found".
: "${SLASH_LSF_SETTINGS:=/path/to/Vivado/settings64.sh}"

# The aved and hls tasks need Vitis rather than Vivado. Vitis also supplies
# bootgen, empyro and the ARM cross compiler, which is what lets the AVED
# firmware build run on a node with nothing SLASH-specific installed.
: "${SLASH_LSF_SETTINGS_aved:=/path/to/Vitis/settings64.sh}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_SETTINGS_hls:=/path/to/Vitis/settings64.sh}"

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- sizing ---

# Site-wide defaults, used by any task without a value of its own.
: "${SLASH_LSF_MEM_MB:=16000}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_CORES:=4}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_WALLTIME:=120}"

# Per-task overrides. The task kinds are static_shell, static_shell_compute,
# rm_slash, rm_service_layer, bootgen, aved, hls and preflight; anything else
# falls back to the site-wide values above.
#
# These numbers are placeholders. Size them from the MAX MEM line of
# "bjobs -l <job_id>" after a real run rather than guessing -- see README.md.

: "${SLASH_LSF_MEM_MB_static_shell:=70000}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_CORES_static_shell:=16}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_WALLTIME_static_shell:=720}"

: "${SLASH_LSF_MEM_MB_static_shell_compute:=70000}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_CORES_static_shell_compute:=16}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_WALLTIME_static_shell_compute:=720}"

: "${SLASH_LSF_MEM_MB_rm_slash:=70000}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_CORES_rm_slash:=16}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_WALLTIME_rm_slash:=720}"

: "${SLASH_LSF_MEM_MB_rm_service_layer:=70000}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_CORES_rm_service_layer:=16}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_WALLTIME_rm_service_layer:=720}"

: "${SLASH_LSF_MEM_MB_bootgen:=4000}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_CORES_bootgen:=1}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_WALLTIME_bootgen:=30}"

: "${SLASH_LSF_MEM_MB_aved:=8000}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_CORES_aved:=4}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_WALLTIME_aved:=60}"

: "${SLASH_LSF_MEM_MB_hls:=16000}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_CORES_hls:=8}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_WALLTIME_hls:=120}"

# preflight.sh only runs a handful of --version calls, so keep it small and
# point it at whatever queue turns jobs around quickest.
: "${SLASH_LSF_QUEUE_preflight:=<your-short-queue>}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_MEM_MB_preflight:=1000}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_CORES_preflight:=1}"
: "${SLASH_LSF_WALLTIME_preflight:=10}"
